    55	## 4. Heading decision for HAA (`tools/exp06_heading.py`)
    56	
    57	The round-1 review showed that a continuous cosine fit is ill-posed on the hallway (training mics lie along ±y: fit −44°, weighted mean −90°, leave-one-out range −147°…−23°) and that an energy-weighted mean conflates directivity with microphone sampling density. The estimator is therefore a **discrete axis decision with stability checks**, and the continuous fits are reported descriptively only.
    58	
    59	Inputs per room (cache `~/data_cache/HAA_xrir/<room>/`): `rirs.npy` (training rows only), `xyzs.npy`, `speaker_xyz.npy`, `meta.json` (`train`, `sr`). **Only the 12 training mics are used.** For training mic `i`: `θ_i = atan2(y_i − y_s, x_i − x_s)`, `d_i = ‖(x_i − x_s, y_i − y_s)‖`, onset `n_i` = first sample with `|h_i| > 0.2·max|h_i|`, compensated level `L_i^(w) = 10 log10(d_i² · Σ_{n=n_i}^{n_i + N_w − 1} h_i[n]²)` with `N_w = int(w·sr)` (floor; **110** and **1102** samples at 22 050 Hz — frozen, tested) for two windows `w ∈ {5 ms, 50 ms}`.
    60	
    61	- **Candidates**: the four axis headings `φ ∈ {0, +90°, 180°, −90°}` (physical prior: the loudspeaker was placed facing along a room axis; the model quantises headings anyway). A candidate is **evaluable** if ≥ 3 training mics lie within ±45° of it and ≥ 3 lie outside that sector. Its **contrast** = mean `L^(w)` inside − mean `L^(w)` outside.
    62	- **Decision**: the evaluable candidate with the largest contrast, required to satisfy all of: contrast ≥ 3 dB (both windows); ≥ 3 dB above every other evaluable candidate (both windows) — **a singleton evaluable candidate is allowed** and recorded with `competitor_count = 0`, `runner_up_margin_db = null` (classroom and complex are singletons: only −y has ≥ 3 mics inside and ≥ 3 outside); the same winner for both windows; the same winner, re-applying all thresholds, when any single training mic is left out (12 leave-one-out refits, both windows). Otherwise **refuse** (fail-closed). The decision is an **inferred acoustic axis**, not an independently verified physical loudspeaker orientation; this limitation is stated in the results.
    63	- **Descriptive extras** (reported, never decisive): the continuous cosine fit `L ≈ a + b cos(θ − φ)` on a 0.5° grid with its leave-one-out range, the energy-weighted mean direction, and per-mic `(θ_i, d_i, L_i)`.
    64	- **Override**: `--heading-deg <value> --override-reason "<text>"` (e.g. a documented DiffRIR loudspeaker orientation) is recorded verbatim alongside the estimator's output; the decision then uses the override.
    65	- Output `ckpt/exp06/heading/<room>.json`: `phi_deg`, `k`, `decision` (`estimated`/`override`/`refused`), contrasts per candidate and window, leave-one-out winners, the descriptive fits, sha256 of the four inputs, the tool's source-closure digest, timestamp.
    66	
    67	Verified on the real training rows (Planner probe and round-2 review, independently): all four rooms decide −y (`k = 128`), 12/12 leave-one-out stable in both windows, smallest leave-one-out winning contrast 7.9 dB; contrasts 5 ms / 50 ms: classroom 12.9 / 9.0 (singleton), dampened 11.4 / 8.7 (runner-up margin 17.4 / 13.1), hallway 18.4 / 11.3 (36.8 / 22.6), complex 12.0 / 10.8 (singleton). The reviewed tool must reproduce these numbers (readback test); refusals in a future room stop that room and are escalated (§11).
