    98	`tools/exp06_eval.py` = `tools/exp04_eval.run_exp04(args, model_factory=build_xrir_exp06, metadata=…, manifest_validator=…)` with an exp_06 parser (backbone choices from `BACKBONES_EXP06`), launched by `tools/exp06_eval_launch.py`: own `parse_args`; **exp_06-specific bindings (`train_completion`, `heading`) are validated and hashed by the exp_06 launcher itself and removed from the argument list before delegating** to `exp04_eval_launch.build_fields(module=exp06_eval)` (which accepts only exp_04's binding names and records `tools.exp04_eval_launch` as writer); the exp_06 launcher then **adds its own closure record** (`writer_exp06 = source_closure('tools.exp06_eval_launch', repo)`) and the exp_06 bindings to the fields, revalidates the manifest, and runs the child through `execute_run`; fields also carry `checkpoint_role`, `checkpoint_epoch`, `heading = none`, registry digest (as `tools/exp05_eval.py` does). Manifests `ckpt/yaw_aug/reference_manifest_k8_seed{42..46}.json`, `--conditions P`, k = 0 only, TF32 off, canonical batch 16, per-query Griffin-Lim seed = manifest seed, full ordered unseen split (6337 queries). Outputs `ckpt/exp06/sim_eval/<arm>/seed<S>/`. **Arm A** already has the five confirmatory K = 8, k = 0 evaluations from exp_04 (`ckpt/yaw_aug/eval/control_k8_seed{42..46}_k0/`, `completion.json` present, same evaluator and manifests); they are admitted through the reused-run branch of §6.4 (approved exp_04 evaluator/writer identities). **Arm B** is taken from exp_05's M-tier evaluations if they exist and pass the same admission when needed; otherwise exp_06 evaluates the exp_01 cylindrical checkpoint itself (≈ 8 min per seed, ≈ 40 min).
