   100	### 6.4 Approvals and admission (mirrors exp_04/exp_05)
   101	
   102	`tools/exp06_profiles.py` + `oriented_cyl_results_assets/approved_digests.json` (null template until filled) has **three sections with separate fill times**: (i) `code` — source-closure digests of `tools.exp06_train`, `tools.exp06_finalize` (+ the shell files `tools/exp06_launch.sh`, `tools/exp06_haa_pipeline.sh` bound as files, below), `model.cylindrical_vit_oriented` + `model.xRIR_cyl_oriented`, `tools.exp06_heading`, `tools.exp06_recipe`, `tools.exp06_probe_align`, `tools.exp06_eval`, `tools.exp06_eval_launch`, `tools.exp06_haa_finetune`, `tools.exp06_haa_eval`, `tools.exp06_mirror_probe`, `tools.exp06_summarize_haa`, `tools.exp06_bootstrap`, `tools.exp06_compare`, plus the pinned exp_03 evaluator digest — **filled before any confirmatory execution** (second reviewed commit); (ii) `reused` — the exp_04 evaluator/writer closure digests and the sha256 of exp_04's and exp_05's `approved_digests.json` as they stand when exp_06 admits the reused A (and possibly B) simulated evaluations, and the exp_02 record identity (canonical `stats.json`/`summary.txt` sha256) for the legacy HAA arms — filled at the same time; (iii) `artifacts` — the `epoch_012.pth` sha256 (path, epoch), the four heading JSON sha256s, the G1 JSON sha256 — **filled after the artifacts exist** (bookkeeping commit verified by the Reviewer). **Lifecycle:** entry points write `provenance.json`; the external finalizer (`tools/exp06_finalize.py`, invoked by `tools/exp06_launch.sh` and `tools/exp06_haa_pipeline.sh` after each child) owns child-exit status, closed-log, input-revalidation and schema checks and writes `completion.json`; **completion units for HAA** are exclusive per-child directories `stage1/`, `stage2_<room>/`, `eval/<room>/` (each with its own `args.json` and `completion.json`) plus one orchestrator-owned job-level `completion.json` under `seed<s>/` after all children finish. **Legacy A/B admission branch:** the historical exp_02 runs have no `completion.json`, heading or closure records; they are admitted through exp_02's own completeness and pairing checks (`summarize_haa.completeness`/pairing assertions, unchanged code) plus an exp_06-owned **hash receipt** over the retained artifacts (`args.json`, `summary.json`, `metrics_*.json`, `per_sample_*.json` per stage/eval, and the canonical `stats.json`/`summary.txt`), written once by `tools/exp06_summarize_haa.py --write-legacy-receipt` and labelled `reconstructed`; historical artifacts are never modified. **Completion evidence by run type** (the finalizer dispatches on a `run_type` recorded in `provenance.json`; nothing else is accepted): *full pretraining* — the twelve-epoch contract above; *smoke/probe* — `no_save` contract, peak-memory and timing receipt, explicitly labelled `diagnostic`, never admissible as an arm; *HAA training child* — `args.json`, `history.jsonl`, `summary.json`, `best.pth`/`last.pth` hashes, heading fields; *HAA evaluation child* — `args.json`, `metrics_<room>.json`, `per_sample_<room>.json` hashes, heading and side-label fields; *HAA job* — the required children's `completion.json` hashes (stage 1, four stage-2, four eval) and the explicit zero-shot layout (`zeroshot/eval/<room>/`); *simulated evaluation* — the inherited `eval_manifest.json` + `execute_run` completion contract of exp_04 (no additional in-directory provenance file; the exp_06 launcher's extra fields live in the manifest). **Approval dependencies per producer** (each producer requires the listed keys and never its own future outputs): heading tool → `code`; mirror probe → `code` + `artifacts.epoch_012` + `artifacts.heading`; HAA pipeline children → `code` + `artifacts.epoch_012` + `artifacts.heading`; summariser → `code` + `reused` (incl. `legacy_receipt`) + `artifacts` (all) + job completions; sim evaluation → `code` + `artifacts.epoch_012`; H3 comparer → `code` + `reused` + sim completions; page generators → the summariser's/comparer's hash-bound outputs. **Legacy receipt approval:** `reused.legacy_receipt = {path, sha256}` is approved after the receipt is written; admission verifies the receipt's own hash and every artifact hash it enumerates, and the legacy completeness check loads the **complete historical exp_02 root** (the inherited checker expects exp_02's full run set) before extracting A and B. **Shell orchestration is bound as files:** `tools/exp06_launch.sh` and `tools/exp06_haa_pipeline.sh` are appended to the relevant `closure_record` file lists after the Python import closures are collected (exp_04's launcher pattern), since `source_closure` imports Python modules only. Every producer refuses (fail-closed, deviations listed) unless the recorded digests match the approved ones, the required run directories are complete, and inputs are bound.
